Subject: [PATCH] package/libvirt: S92libvirtd: test for the vfio directory

load_modules() tests that each directory exists before searching it for
modules, but the test before the search of drivers/vfio is for
drivers/net, the directory of the search before it. With a kernel that
has modules in drivers/net but none in drivers/vfio (VFIO disabled or
built in), find prints at every start:

  Loading kernel modules: find: /lib/modules/<version>/kernel/drivers/vfio: No such file or directory

Test for drivers/vfio, as the other two tests do for the directory they
search.

Present in 2026.08.1 and master.
---
--- a/package/libvirt/S92libvirtd
+++ b/package/libvirt/S92libvirtd
@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@
 	[ -d "/lib/modules/$kver/kernel/drivers/vhost" ] && \
 		find "/lib/modules/$kver/kernel/drivers/vhost" \
 		-name "vhost?net.ko*" >> "$TMP_MODULE_LIST"
-	[ -d "/lib/modules/$kver/kernel/drivers/net" ] && \
+	[ -d "/lib/modules/$kver/kernel/drivers/vfio" ] && \
 		find "/lib/modules/$kver/kernel/drivers/vfio" \
 		-name "*.ko*" >> "$TMP_MODULE_LIST"
 	while read -r f; do
